 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5524+) Rearrange Advisor **keyboard shortcuts** (in [CIV4ControlInfos.xml](/Assets/XML/Units/CIV4ControlInfos.xml) and DLL files like [CvEnums.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEnums.h), [CvEnums.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEnums.h), [CvGameInterface.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvGameInterface.cpp), and [CyEnumsInterface.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CyEnumsInterface.cpp)) and adjust the **order of advisor buttons** in map view and **Sevopedia shortcuts** corresponding text to match the advisors changes.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5521+) **Expand** and most **advisors** so they scale to **game resolution dynamically** instead of hardcoded advisor screen dimensions. The code was also refactored to improve **dynamic scaling**, ensuring **most UI elements automatically realign** if dimensions are changed. Advisors are now **excentered** so **overall more information** is displayed, thus **reducing the need for scrolling**, while still **preserving key relevant information** for display (scoreboard, map, commerce sliders and values, etc.). Some of their dimensions are **harmonized**. Note: some **right space for scoreboard** and **top space for the top bars** of the main interface was made (since commerce sliders are now as of now on the right side, they don't need left space anymore). See [Main Advisors reworks](/README.md#main-advisors-reworks-eg-score-tab-timeline-tab-in-the-info-screen-advisor)
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5521+) **Expand** and most **advisors** so they scale to **game resolution dynamically** instead of hardcoded advisor screen dimensions. The code was also refactored to improve **dynamic scaling**, ensuring **most UI elements automatically realign** if dimensions are changed. Advisors are now **excentered** so **overall more information** is displayed, thus **reducing the need for scrolling**, while still **preserving key relevant information** for display (scoreboard, map, commerce sliders and values, etc.). Some of their dimensions are **harmonized**. Note: some **right space for scoreboard** and **top space for the top bars** of the main interface was made (since commerce sliders are now as of now on the right side, they don't need left space anymore). See [Main Advisors reworks](/README.md#main-advisors-reworks-eg-new-world-advisor-score-tab-and-timeline-tab-in-the-info-screen-advisor)
 - **Beautified** the **Domestic Advisor**: now shows the **button (i.e. icon) of the current item being built** (unit, building, project, process) in "Producing" column. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5522+) Use the **shared advisor shell layout** (**top/bottom bars** + single content panel, remove the old exit icon) so Domestic Advisor **mirrors other advisors' structure** instead of a floating table, now using a **clearer constrast dark yellow theme** instead. Make the advisor be a tab as the **Overview** tab. Change in [CvDomesticAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDomesticAdvisor.py).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5528+) Minor **beautified** the [CvCustomizableDomesticAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvCustomizableDomesticAdvisor.py): increase **legend culture text width** so it is not cramped when upscaled. Note: although it is functional, the Custom Domestic Advisor is **not supported** in AdvCiv-SAS as of now, so it is lacking the Finance Tab.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5522+) **Beautified** the **Policy Advisor**: enlarge **top panels text** so **long civic names don't overflow**. **Remove multiline nationality** information which was **uninfomative** and **crowded vertically** in the **Religions tab** and the **Corporations tab**; use more precise and compact `Leader (ID)` and `HQ (ID)` **one-liner instead** (**ID** also handles **one leader name being used by several players**); **increase row spacing** (now **unified** (was crowded)). **Remove multiline wrapped bonuses** splitting logic in the **Corporations tab**: use one natural comma-separated line (bonuses row height reduced/standardized) since there is enough space after expanding the Policy Advisor and it is more readable. Also add **new rows** (**Bonuses Generated**, **Yields Generated**), and add **first column descriptions** for rows (as of now `Built By:`, `Consumes:`, `Generates:`, `Generates 2:`). Add a **Great Person icon** in `Built By:` row. Change in [CvPolicyAdvisorScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvPolicyAdvisorScreen.py).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5522+) New **Policy Advisor**. **Beautified**: enlarge **top panels text** so **long civic names don't overflow**. **Remove multiline nationality** information which was **uninfomative** and **crowded vertically** in the **Religions tab** and the **Corporations tab**; use more precise and compact `Leader (ID)` and `HQ (ID)` **one-liner instead** (**ID** also handles **one leader name being used by several players**); **increase row spacing** (now **unified** (was crowded)). **Remove multiline wrapped bonuses** splitting logic in the **Corporations tab**: use one natural comma-separated line (bonuses row height reduced/standardized) since there is enough space after expanding the Policy Advisor and it is more readable. Also add **new rows** (**Bonuses Generated**, **Yields Generated**), and add **first column descriptions** for rows (as of now `Built By:`, `Consumes:`, `Generates:`, `Generates 2:`). Add a **Great Person icon** in `Built By:` row. Change in [CvPolicyAdvisorScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvPolicyAdvisorScreen.py).
 - **Foreign Advisor**: refined its tabs so they can display **up to 12 players**. Notably renamed the Active tab to **Treaties** tab (no longer shows redundant bonuses (since their deal can be cancelled from the bonuses tab)), and **beautified** it with **icons**. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5516+) Always use the unified **table-style info layout** (`drawInfoImproved`) for the Info Tab for stable column behavior: the old hardcoded text spacing (`drawInfoOriginal`) did not **scale with upscaled font text** nor **adjust depending on advisor screen size**. Plus the improved layout has additional **information** like general or specific **colored leader attitude text** related to civic/religion choices (e.g., `[-2]` or `[+1]`). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5518+) **Beautified** the **Espionage Tab** similarly; notably **removed redundant Espionage slider** now that commerce sliders are on the right side of main interface in map view, and **improved text spacing** that **was colliding or overflowing** beyond its panel, and **moved + - buttons under the leader icon** where there is more room and it is more intuitive and easier to click it.
 - Added **"Willing to become vassal"** and **"Vassal"** **icons** in the Foreign Advisor's Glance tab in the human player's row, to help avoid the need to tediously check these up through other screens, in [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py), and in [CvDLLWidgetData.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDLLWidgetData.cpp) for the corresponding **tooltip** (on hover). See ["Willing to become a vassal" and "vassal" icons](/README.md#willing-to-become-a-vassal-and-vassal-icons-in-foreign-advisors-glance-tab).
 - Reworked the **Military Advisor** in [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py) now with Unit Combat and Units **icons**. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5530+) Note: **icon size** is **increased** at **higher resolutions** (e.g., from 24 to 32 if resolution height >= 1440). Note 2: as of now the [CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py) is not supported.
 - Similarly Beautified and Enhanced the **Technology Advisor** in [CvTechChooser.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvTechChooser.py) so it uses more of the screen while still preserving key information. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5519+) Players can **optionally** set an **alternative lower right space for scoreboard** on **lower game resolutions** (e.g., 1920*1080) so that an **extra column or more is visible** in the technology advisor, and an **alternative top space space** for **advisor buttons** (in map view) because this alternative right space may cover these advisor buttons. **Boldened title** for consistency. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5520+) See also [KI#114](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#114---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-tech-advisor-on-save-load-initially-shown-current-tech-missing-turns-left-timer-until-another-tech-is-clicked). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5691+) **When opening** Technology Advisor, **right-align scoreboard leader text** so it is easier to read (because text is often not visible due to advisor width expansion). **On Technology Advisor close**, it **reverts back** to usual alignment.
 - **Inverted BUG Options** for the **Technology Advisor** and the **Religion Advisor** so they are more accessible. They are now **enabled as a default**, and ticking their box disables them. Rewrote their text for clarity (e.g. "GP Research" -> **"Hide bulbing indicators"**). See [Inverted BUG options](/README.md#inverted-bug-options).
-- Did a similar rework of the **Info Screen** in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py); in particular in **Top 5 Cities** we now use a multilist to display more wonders in a prettier way, and in the **Wonders** tab we now **show the Wonders' Buttons** (i.e. icons) in the first column (**click to move to city** mechanic is moved to the City column instead); the **Statistics** tab now also shows buttons (plus **change default ordering** from alphabetical to **from most to least Built/Current** (avoids tedious manual user ordering each time)), and the **Graph** Tab and possibly other tabs also show buttons (e.g., **leader icons before text**, **emojis**). Also added other information (e.g., turn numbers in the Graph tab).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5522+) New **World Advisor**: shows **detailed BFC, suburbs, and territory geography** information as **sortable tables**. BFC tabs show information **per city (rows)** and **per field (columns)**, and have a **click to enter city button** (similar to the Info Screen's Wonders tab). The BFC1 tab shows mostly **plot type** and **terrains/features** information; the BFC2 tab shows mostly **bonuses** and **improvements** information. The Territory tab shows a **condensed summary** with 4 tables of the former BFC tabs, with a BFC, suburbs (i.e. plots outside BFC) and **Total counts (columns)** for each field (rows), with **hover support** and **pedia redirect on click** (if a corresponding pedia page exists), and a legend link. The **environment tab** is now part of the World advisor (better thematic fit).
+- Did a similar rework of the **Info Screen** in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py); in particular in **Top 5 Cities** we now use a multilist to display more wonders in a prettier way, and in the **Wonders** tab we now **show the Wonders' Buttons** (i.e. icons) in the first column (**click to move to city** mechanic is moved to the City column instead); the **Statistics** tab now also shows buttons (plus **change default ordering** from alphabetical to **from most to least Built** (avoids tedious manual user ordering each time)), and the **Graph** Tab and possibly other tabs also show buttons (e.g., **leader icons before text**, **emojis**). Also added other information (e.g., turn numbers in the Graph tab). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5718+) **Removed** the **Improvements table** from the Statistics tab, because it was **inconsistent** with how Units and Buidings show all-time total **built**, Improvements would only show **current** possession (e.g., building a farm, replacing it with a cottage, then replacing it again with a farm would be Current 1 farm, not total built 2 farms), plus the World Advisor is a **better thematic fit**.
 - Additionally, added in the **Info Screen** a new **Timeline Tab**, showing a **text-colored spoiler-free** account of the key moments that happened each turn. Based on the **ReplayScreen**'s text, so **preserves information on save reload** unlike the Event Log. Optional **LOG button** allows to export to `PythonDbg.log` text file the output, and has optional **caching** for performance. Change in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py). See [README.md: Timeline Tab](/README.md#timeline-tab-in-the-info-screen-advisor).
 - Added in the **Info Screen** a new **Score Tab** showing a **sortable (default ordered by highest score) table** with all relevant scoreboard fields, plus **new fields** like Player color, Player ID (to distinguish identical Name/Civ/Leader/Player Color), (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5532+) Traits (T1 and T2) as **icon chars**, total Power (of a player, distinct from power ratios), total Power per City, Land%, V/M, Tech (total techs). Added a clickable **"Legend"** text that **redirects to Sevopedia Concepts' "Score Tab Columns" page**. Note that unlike military ratios, PowT and PoT/C are shown even for the human player, since these vary every turn. Change in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py). See [README.md: Score Tab](/README.md#score-tab-in-the-info-screen-advisor).
 - Beautified the **Victory Screen**: **added Buttons/Icons** (Leaders, Religions, Apostolic Palace, UN, Spaceship parts, Traits as chars, etc.), **Thousands Separators**, **Victory Culture Percentages** (mirroring the changes in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py)). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5523+) **Always show** the **Resolutions** and **Members** tabs so now all tabs are shown **even if they are empty**, and add a **fallback table** showing **required wonders** (as of now Apostolic Palace or United Nations) to make these tabs active for exhaustiveness and clarity. Change in [CvVictoryScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvVictoryScreen.py). See also [KI#115](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#115---fixed-likely-base-advciv-issue-victory-screen-vote-requirement-text-spacing-in-resolutions-tab).

